#UML SEQUENCE DIAGRAM
```mermaid```
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant Client as Client Node
    participant JointSrv as Joint Configuration Server
    participant RSP as robot_state_publisher / RViz
    participant TF2 as TF2 Buffer / Tree
    participant PoseSrv as End-Effector Pose Server

    User->>Client: Run from terminal with joint args<br/>(ros2 run pkg client <j1 j2 ...>)
    
    Note over Client, JointSrv: Service Call 1: Set Joint Configuration
    Client->>+JointSrv: Request: SetJointConfig(joint_values)
    JointSrv->>JointSrv: Validate values against joint limits

    alt Joint values are VALID
        JointSrv--)RSP: Publish: /joint_states (sensor_msgs/JointState)
        Note right of RSP: Updates RViz visualization<br/>& computes kinematics
        RSP--)TF2: Broadcast: /tf (base_frame -> end_effector)
        JointSrv-->>Client: Response: success = True, message = "OK"
    else Joint values are OUT OF LIMITS
        JointSrv-->>-Client: Response: success = False, message = "Limit exceeded..."
    end

    opt If Joint Configuration Succeeded (success == True)
        Note over Client, PoseSrv: Service Call 2: Query End-Effector Pose
        Client->>+PoseSrv: Request: GetEndEffectorPose()
        PoseSrv->>+TF2: lookup_transform(base_frame, end_effector)
        
        alt Transform found in TF2
            TF2-->>PoseSrv: Return TransformStamped
            PoseSrv-->>Client: Response: success = True, pose = Pose
            Client->>User: Print returned end-effector pose
        else TF2 LookupException / Timeout
            TF2-->>-PoseSrv: Raise TF2 Exception
            PoseSrv-->>-Client: Response: success = False, pose = Empty
            Client->>User: Print error message
        end
    end
